(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["transitions_10"] = [{"id":"90117366","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"To explore how blinking affects social interactions, Dutch researchers observed interactions between human speakers and “listeners” (animated human faces on a screen). The researchers found that when the listeners blinked slowly, the speakers tended to talk for less time. ______ quicker blinks were associated with longer talking times.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"To explore how blinking affects social interactions, Dutch researchers observed interactions between human speakers and “listeners” (animated","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"human faces on a screen). The researchers found that when the listeners blinked slowly, the speakers tended to talk for less time. ______ quicker","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"blinks were associated with longer talking times.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For example,","Specifically,","Firstly,","By contrast,"]},{"id":"827afb27","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Most conifers (trees belonging to the phylum Coniferophyta) are evergreen. That is, they keep their green leaves or needles year-round. However, not all conifer species are evergreen. Larch trees, ______ lose their needles every fall.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Most conifers (trees belonging to the phylum Coniferophyta)are evergreen. That is, they keep their green leaves or needles year-round. However,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"not all conifer species are evergreen. Larch trees, ______ lose their needles every fall.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["for instance,","nevertheless,","meanwhile,","in addition,"]},{"id":"c7e85c0a","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The envelope-shaped paper bags common in the US 150 years ago were impractical for carrying goods. ______ because they were the only paper bags that could be mass-produced, these bags dominated the market. That all changed in the 1870s, when industrial designer Margaret Knight patented a machine to make flat-bottomed, foldable paper bags.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The envelope-shaped paper bags common in the US 150 years ago were impractical for carrying goods. ______ because they were the only paper","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"bags that could be mass-produced, these bags dominated the market. That all changed in the 1870s, when industrial designer Margaret Knight","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"patented a machine to make flat-bottomed, foldable paper bags.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["However,","For instance,","Thus,","In other words,"]},{"id":"6916c8e5","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Laetitia Ky’s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds of shapes. ______ she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa —including the island of Madagascar!","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Laetitia Ky’s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of shapes. ______ she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa—including the island of Madagascar!","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Soon,","Elsewhere,","For example,","However,"]},{"id":"9c78f702","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Phytoplankton play a crucial role in the ocean’s uptake of carbon from the atmosphere. When alive, these tiny marine organisms absorb atmospheric carbon via photosynthesis. ______ after they die, the phytoplankton sink to the seafloor, where the carbon in their cells gets stored in sediment, preventing it from cycling back into the atmosphere.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Phytoplankton play a crucial role in the ocean’s uptake of carbon from the atmosphere. When alive, these tiny marine organisms absorb","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"atmospheric carbon via photosynthesis. ______ after they die, the phytoplankton sink to the seafloor, where the carbon in their cells gets stored in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sediment, preventing it from cycling back into the atmosphere.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Specifically,","By contrast,","Nevertheless,","Then,"]},{"id":"74028acf","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Topographic maps show the elevation of landforms above sea level. Bathymetric maps, ______ show the elevation of landforms below the sea, providing valuable information to marine geophysicists like Claudia Flores, who studies seismic data from the northeastern Caribbean.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Topographic maps show the elevation of landforms above sea level. Bathymetric maps, ______ show the elevation of landforms below the sea,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"providing valuable information to marine geophysicists like Claudia Flores, who studies seismic data from the northeastern Caribbean.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["in conclusion,","for example,","by contrast,","afterward,"]},{"id":"332e75bf","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In Annie Dillard’s Pilgrim at Tinker Creek — where, early on, the author marvels at a single goldfish’s delicate fins but later winces when imagining a horde of goldfish laying and eating their own eggs — Dillard struggles to reconcile the complicated juxtapositions of the natural world. ______ nature’s mesmerizing intricacy and pitiless harshness prove inextricably linked for Dillard, like “two branches of the same creek.”","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In Annie Dillard’s Pilgrim at Tinker Creek—where, early on, the author marvels at a single goldfish’s delicate fins but later winces when imagining a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"horde of goldfish laying and eating their own eggs—Dillard struggles to reconcile the complicated juxtapositions of the natural world. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"nature’s mesmerizing intricacy and pitiless harshness prove inextricably linked for Dillard, like “two branches of the same creek.”","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["To that end,","Ultimately,","Moreover,","Hence,"]},{"id":"42870a4e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Marcel Duchamp intended his 1917 so-called ready-made sculpture Fountain to challenge then-prevailing conceptions about the nature of art. ______ Duchamp’s Fountain did just that, raising the question of whether displaying any object in an art gallery could be said to transform the object — even, as Duchamp’s sculpture was, a urinal — into a legitimate work of art.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Marcel Duchamp intended his 1917 so-called ready-made sculpture Fountain to challenge then-prevailing conceptions about the nature of art.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ Duchamp’s Fountain did just that, raising the question of whether displaying any object in an art gallery could be said to transform the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"object—even, as Duchamp’s sculpture was, a urinal—into a legitimate work of art.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","Indeed,","Instead,","In addition,"]},{"id":"0205e563","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"At two weeks old, the time their critical socialization period begins, wolves can smell but cannot yet see or hear. Domesticated dogs, ______ can see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks. This relative lack of sensory input may help explain why wolves behave so differently around humans than dogs do: from a very young age, wolves are more wary and less exploratory.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"At two weeks old, the time their critical socialization period begins, wolves can smell but cannot yet see or hear. Domesticated dogs, ______ can","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"see, hear, and smell by the end of two weeks. This relative lack of sensory input may help explain why wolves behave so differently around","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"humans than dogs do: from a very young age, wolves are more wary and less exploratory.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["in other words,","for instance,","by contrast,","accordingly,"]},{"id":"6a5939c2","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Paleontologists once thought that early apes lived in tropical forests, but recent research suggests that they may have actually lived in savannas. Tropical forests are humid and have many trees spaced close together. ______ savannas are drier, and their trees are spaced further apart.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Paleontologists once thought that early apes lived in tropical forests, but recent research suggests that they may have actually lived in savannas.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Tropical forests are humid and have many trees spaced close together. ______ savannas are drier, and their trees are spaced further apart.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For instance,","In comparison,","Firstly,","In conclusion,"]},{"id":"57bcd0d6","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Etched into Peru’s Nazca Desert are line drawings so large that they can only be fully seen from high above. Archaeologists have known of the lines since the 1920s, when a researcher spotted some from a nearby foothill, and they have been studying the markings ever since. ______ archaeologists’ efforts are aided by drones that capture high-resolution aerial photographs of the lines.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Etched into Peru’s Nazca Desert are line drawings so large that they can only be fully seen from high above. Archaeologists have known of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"lines since the 1920s, when a researcher spotted some from a nearby foothill, and they have been studying the markings ever since. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"archaeologists’ efforts are aided by drones that capture high-resolution aerial photographs of the lines.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Currently,","In comparison,","Still,","However,"]},{"id":"4b7a84b0","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Mountain climbing routes that incorporate metal rungs and cables are known as via ferratas, from the Italian phrase for iron path. As climbing these routes has shifted from a mode of travel to a sporting activity, modern via ferratas are rarely designed to simply reach a summit. ______ new routes favor recreation over utility, aiming to provide a challenging climb or showcase dramatic scenery.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Mountain climbing routes that incorporate metal rungs and cables are known as via ferratas, from the Italian phrase for “iron path.” As climbing","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"these routes has shifted from a mode of travel to a sporting activity, modern via ferratas are rarely designed to simply reach a summit. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"new routes favor recreation over utility, aiming to provide a challenging climb or showcase dramatic scenery.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Additionally,","On the other hand,","More often,","Nonetheless,"]},{"id":"de0bcf4f","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Spanish surrealist Oscar Dominguez, like many of his contemporaries, wanted to incorporate elements of chance and randomness in his artistic process. ______ he employed techniques that produced random, unpredictable results, such as decalcomania, which involved pressing a blank canvas onto a paint-covered surface to generate abstract patterns.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Spanish surrealist Oscar Dominguez, like many of his contemporaries, wanted to incorporate elements of chance and randomness in his artistic","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"process. ______ he employed techniques that produced random, unpredictable results, such as decalcomania, which involved pressing a blank","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"canvas onto a paint-covered surface to generate abstract patterns.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["With this in mind,","On the contrary,","In conclusion,","Regardless,"]},{"id":"20e4ff59","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Famous for its four-degree tilt, the leaning Garisenda Tower is a popular attraction in Bologna’s city center. However, measurements taken in 2023 showed that the tower was rotating in a concerning way. ______ city officials closed the area around the tower so experts could explore solutions to stabilize the historical twelfth-century structure.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Famous for its four-degree tilt, the leaning Garisenda Tower is a popular attraction in Bologna’s city center. However, measurements taken in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"2023 showed that the tower was rotating in a concerning way. ______ city officials closed the area around the tower so experts could explore","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"solutions to stabilize the historical twelfth-century structure.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","As a result,","For example,","In comparison,"]},{"id":"a3bf0a9d","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In 2021, a model developed by astrophysicist Catherine Zucker and her research team revealed that the same supernovas responsible for the creation and ongoing expansion of the Local Bubble — a 14-million-year-old cavity in the Milky Way — are likely responsible for the formation of new stars. ______ this model detailed how the bubble’s expansion trapped interstellar clouds of gas and dust that became stars upon their eventual collapse.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 2021, a model developed by astrophysicist Catherine Zucker and her research team revealed that the same supernovas responsible for the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"creation and ongoing expansion of the Local Bubble—a 14-million-year-old cavity in the Milky Way—are likely responsible for the formation of new","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"stars. ______ this model detailed how the bubble’s expansion trapped interstellar clouds of gas and dust that became stars upon their eventual","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"collapse.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Hence,","However,","Admittedly,","Specifically,"]}];
